# Copy values into Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# (Do not put secrets here — only public values)

# LEAVE THIS EMPTY.
#
# The API is proxied same-origin through the rewrites in client/vercel.json, so
# the client calls relative paths like /api/auth/login. That is what makes the
# refresh cookie work: it is SameSite=Strict, and a cookie set on the API's own
# host would never be sent from the frontend's host — vercel.app is on the
# Public Suffix List, so client-*.vercel.app and nexora-api-*.vercel.app are
# different sites, not sibling subdomains.
#
# Setting an absolute URL here silently reintroduces that split: requests still
# work, the cookie stops being sent, and every refresh fails with no obvious
# cause. If you move the API to a custom domain, change the destination in
# client/vercel.json instead of setting this.
VITE_API_URL=

# Optional — enables the live notification badge over Supabase Realtime.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...
